        },
        "stem": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Concentrated urine contains a high concentration of solutes and a small volume of water. Different species of mammals vary in their ability to produce urine with a high solute concentration.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 13
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Table 6.1 compares the ratio of the solute concentration of urine (U) to the solute concentration of blood plasma (P) in some mammal species. The habitats of the mammal species are also shown.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 13
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table 6.1",
            "head": [
              "<b>mammal</b> <b>species</b>",
              "<b>maximum</b> <b>ratio</b> <b>of</b><br><b>solute</b> <b>concentration</b> <b>of</b> <b>urine</b><br><b>to</b> <b>solute</b> <b>concentration</b> <b>of</b> <b>blood</b> <b>plasma</b><br><b>(U</b> <b>:</b> <b>P)</b>",
              "<b>habitat</b>"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "beaver",
                "1.7 : 1",
                "rivers and lakes"
              ],
              [
                "human",
                "4.5 : 1",
                "variable"
              ],
              [
                "camel",
                "8.0 : 1",
                "desert"
              ],
              [
                "rat",
                "9.0 : 1",
                "variable"
              ],
              [
                "kangaroo rat",
                "16.0 : 1",
                "desert"
              ]
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With reference to Table 6.1, suggest what the different values of U : P show about the ability of these mammal species to tolerate a shortage of water in their environment.",
            "source": {
              "qp": 13
            }
          }
        ],
        "marks": 3,
        "markScheme": {
          "marks": 3,
          "instruction": "<i>any </i><b><i>three</i></b><i> from: </i>",
          "guidance": [],
          "points": [
            {
              "n": 1,
              "text": "high(er / est), U:P / ratio → can tolerate water shortage <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 2,
              "text": "high(er / est), U:P / ratio → much water reabsorbed / small volume of urine produced <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 3,
              "text": "high(er / est), U:P / ratio → can, concentrate urine / conserve water <b>OR </b>high(er / est), U:P / ratio → (well) adapted to dry environment <b>; </b>"
            },
            {
              "n": 4,
              "text": "AVP<b> ; </b>"
            }
          ]
